{
  "//": [
    "The resolved stack registry, frozen. One entry per preset, in the",
    "order `Object.values(STACKS)` yields them, with every reference",
    "reduced to the id it resolved from — verticals in install order,",
    "build systems and module layouts in offer order, a composite's",
    "services by path + stack id + extra-vertical ids.",
    "",
    "This file was generated from the TypeScript object literals that",
    "held the presets before they became data, and it is the acceptance",
    "test for that move: `keel new --list`, `keel.catalog`, the",
    "drill-down grid and every scaffolded tree read the registry through",
    "these fields, so a registry that still projects onto this file is a",
    "registry nothing observable changed about.",
    "",
    "It stays afterwards for the reason `tests/version-pins.test.ts`",
    "stays: a preset edit that was not meant to be user-visible shows up",
    "here as a diff of what users actually see, in the same review as",
    "the change. Adding or changing a preset means changing this file",
    "too — that is the cost, and it is the point."
  ],
